a. establishing and implementing policies, programs, and activities for the fulfillment of children's rights;
b. providing facilities and infrastructure in the implementation of fulfillment of children's rights;
c. conducting guidance and supervision in the context of implementation of fulfillment of children's rights;
d. respecting and guaranteeing the human rights of every child without discriminating based on ethnicity, religion, race, class, gender, ethnicity, culture and language, legal status of the child, birth order of the child, and physical and/or mental condition; and
e. cooperating with private parties and/or non-governmental organizations in the implementation of fulfillment of children's rights. (2) Regional Government in the context of fulfilling children's rights may cooperate with the community, business sector, and mass media. (3) The responsibility of Regional Government in the effort to fulfill children's rights as referred to in paragraph (1) is implemented by regional apparatus in accordance with their duties and functions.

Article 21

Preventive efforts for basic health services as referred to in Article 19 paragraph (2) letter b shall be implemented in order to prevent the occurrence of disease or health problems carried out by: a. requiring mothers to provide exclusive breast milk to infants until the age of 6 (six) months;

b. providing immunization and vitamins free of charge to infants and toddlers; c. providing nutritious food to infants and toddlers from underprivileged families;

d. providing monitoring of the growth and development of toddlers and preschool-age children;

e. organizing comprehensive health efforts for children; 14

f. optimizing the role of integrated service posts in serving maternal and child health; and

g. providing sanitation facilities and clean water at every school.

