c. requiring intensive services but their residence is relatively far; and/or
d. neglected if not placed in a safe house.

Article 38

(1) The Regional Government in the effort to provide special protection for children is responsible for:

a. providing facilities and infrastructure in implementing special protection for children;
b. providing access to public services and social services for children with disabilities;
c. establishing and implementing policies and programs/activities for special protection of children;
d. conducting cooperation with the community and/or community organizations in implementing special protection for children in accordance with laws and regulations;
e. conducting rehabilitation and assistance for children who become victims of violence;
f. providing special protection to children in emergency situations, children in conflict with the law, child victims of acts of violence and human trafficking, children from minority and isolated groups, children exploited economically and/or sexually, children who become victims of narcotics, alcohol, psychotropics abuse, and HIV/AIDS;
g. providing inclusive education for children with special needs; and
h. taking preventive measures in order to prevent violations of children's rights.
